MODULE main

START APPLICATION
    create renderer, camera, landscape material, post-processing, and default settings
    create colour state and editor readouts
    restore saved landscape when browser storage contains a valid design
    create explained controls for camera, terrain, editor, environment, bloom, and colours
    listen for canvas clicks and window resizing
    continuously render the scene

ON CANVAS CLICK AT screen position
    if all rock slots are occupied
        report the rock limit
        return
    calculate the world ray for the clicked canvas position
    find the terrain point intersected by that ray
    if the ray misses terrain
        report that visible ground must be clicked
        return
    place the next rock above the terrain point
    update the rock-count readout
    save the landscape and report the terrain point

CREATE LANDSCAPE DATA
    collect camera position and look-at point
    collect terrain, environment, bloom, and colour settings
    collect occupied rock positions
    validate and return the complete Landscape

APPLY LANDSCAPE data
    validate all data before changing application state
    apply camera, terrain, environment, bloom, and colour settings
    clear every rock slot
    copy imported rock positions into the available slots
    update preset and rock-count readouts

SAVE LANDSCAPE message
    create validated Landscape data
    write it to browser storage
    report message
    if creation or storage fails
        report the underlying error

RESTORE LANDSCAPE
    read the saved JSON from browser storage
    if no save exists
        keep defaults
    otherwise parse, validate, and apply it
    report restoration or the underlying rejection reason

EXPORT LANDSCAPE
    create validated Landscape data
    download it as formatted JSON
    refresh browser storage
    report export or the underlying failure

IMPORT SELECTED LANDSCAPE FILE
    read and parse the selected JSON file
    validate the complete Landscape before changing the scene
    apply it and refresh every control
    save it in browser storage
    report the filename or the underlying failure

CLEAR ROCKS
    empty every rock slot
    update Rock Count
    save the landscape

FORGET AUTOSAVE
    remove the browser storage entry
    leave the visible landscape unchanged
    report the result
